e\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:brief:'first-time volunteers' is one line on w\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:code:counts passed as a JSON string, which js\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:brief:footer has a 70-character cap the brief\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:visual:Following the tutorial's own week.json p\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:brief:30-build.md says ten clubs at 1280x720 m\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:code:Whether milestone clubs fit depends on t\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:visual:Milestone badge counts are never checked\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:brief:With footer \\\"\\\" the freed height goes int\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:code:Sanity checks miss newPbs + firstTimers\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:visual:On every wide canvas the milestone club\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:visual:Caveat and outputHints say only ten club\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"review:code\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Review\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"review:visual\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Review\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}{\"agentType\":\"workflow-subagent\",\"description\":\"verify:brief:The WHY 'Use it' example renders a real\",\"workflowPhase\":\"Verify\",\"spawnDepth\":1,\"requestShape\":\"foreground\",\"requestNonInteractive\":true}\n{\"type\":\"launched\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:8fc7b78a67a4580a12887a02e6500cdacec08a685c6d22cc93f7e42e4075146e\",\"agentId\":\"ac77a509872f6adb4\",\"label\":\"review:code\",\"phase\":\"Review\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:258c8d1ff81fcf696c07c5c18a0521cd4b49a43a79c6f5b1978f9c4ff4ea9abc\",\"agentId\":\"a0e88aa623c3be9de\",\"label\":\"review:brief\",\"phase\":\"Review\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:51485f052245b3716ae7def30f7083582a4053b50bc04dddb96182ac4f6243f0\",\"agentId\":\"ac914dc551f41cb2b\",\"label\":\"review:visual\",\"phase\":\"Review\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"key\":\"v2:51485f052245b3716ae7def30f7083582a4053b50bc04dddb96182ac4f6243f0\",\"agentId\":\"ac914dc551f41cb2b\",\"result\":{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"A misspelled top-level prop silently puts the sample week's invented numbers on a real card, which is the exact failure the header comment says the template prevents\",\"file\":\"C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day/src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts\",\"repro\":\"I rendered `m0saic make @one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/typo.props.json -o journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/typo.png`. The props are {\\\"eventName\\\":\\\"Riverside 5k\\\",\\\"runNumber\\\":88,\\\"date\\\":\\\"2026-10-10\\\",\\\"count\\\":{\\\"finishers\\\":120,...},\\\"milestone\\\":\\\"1xR50\\\",\\\"footer\\\":\\\"Thank you to all our volunteers\\\"}, so `count` and `milestone` are misspelled.\\n\\nWhat happens: exit 0 with no warning. The card reads RIVERSIDE 5K #88 SAT 10 OCT 2026 with 214 finishers, 31 volunteers, 38/27/19/4 and badges 25 '4 runners', 50 '3 runners', 100 '1 runner', 25 '2 volunteers'. Every one of those is invented sample data, and the custom footer means nothing on the card says 'sample'.\\n\\nWhy it happens: `normalizeWeeklyRunReport` (line 273) merges DEFAULTS with the props and never rejects an unknown top-level key. Leaving `counts` out entirely has the same effect.\\n\\nWhat was promised: header comment lines 26-30 say 'the card prints what was typed and nothing else... a silently ignored typo puts a wrong number on a public page'. The missing-key error says 'The card never invents a number.' Expected: refuse an unknown prop name (or at least refuse when counts or milestones fall back to the sample values while eventName or runNumber are the user's own).\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"suggestedFix\":\"In normalizeWeeklyRunReport, refuse any top-level key not in the schema, naming it (e.g. \\\"unknown prop 'count'; did you mean 'counts'?\\\"). Also refuse a counts or milestones that falls back to DEFAULTS when eventName or runNumber differs from the sample, or have the header comment and WHY admit that defaults fill in for missing props.\"},{\"title\":\"Following the tutorial's own week.json prints run #313 with the sample week's date and the 'Sample week: event and numbers are invented' footer\",\"file\":\"C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day/src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts\",\"repro\":\"WHY.usage.try[0] (line 687, shown on tutorial-4.png) suggests week.json: {\\\"eventName\\\":\\\"Your Park 5k\\\",\\\"runNumber\\\":313,\\\"counts\\\":{...},\\\"milestones\\\":\\\"2xR25, 1xV50\\\"}. I filled in counts (journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/tutorial-week.props.json) and rendered at 1080x1080 to journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/tutorial-week.png.\\n\\nWhat the card shows: '#313 | SAT 03 OCT 2026', which is the default date of sample run #312, a week too early. The footer says 'Sample week: event and numbers are invented' under the user's real numbers.\\n\\nWhat was claimed: the date was never typed\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:403289cb46488299691ab3af7d5b43f17942fb2df9dce1cd5812eeab7cc241cd\",\"agentId\":\"a3b07ed1f1db4a43b\",\"label\":\"verify:visual:A misspelled top-level prop silently put\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:191729cb51caf5050ca1585e68067052cffde730c525cd020347eb5738278aac\",\"agentId\":\"a6abad53693714aa1\",\"label\":\"verify:visual:Following the tutorial's own week.json p\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:8e42e7d2ab785e7892800a6e217d8399be8c9a81b5dc76fe47006b1411903343\",\"agentId\":\"a79c927819aed729f\",\"label\":\"verify:visual:Milestone badge counts are never checked\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:0ec19ed1f383a89cc4ad82abc668b99b5edfe78ae97af10286b6446b32e1ada2\",\"agentId\":\"a0a658a69efa91c47\",\"label\":\"verify:visual:30-build.md describes the ten and long s\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:a7730e33bb85990f38e76376d914b680104256658c14762c06a5252e6624fc55\",\"agentId\":\"aadb4847ab36ac6c9\",\"label\":\"verify:visual:Caveat and outputHints say only ten club\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:6cb63f45c121dcfbe1c04163b514795d755231017731092dc3ce412ba85b1859\",\"agentId\":\"aa94bcf16362dba09\",\"label\":\"verify:visual:On every wide canvas the milestone club\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"key\":\"v2:0ec19ed1f383a89cc4ad82abc668b99b5edfe78ae97af10286b6446b32e1ada2\",\"agentId\":\"a0a658a69efa91c47\",\"result\":{\"real\":true,\"evidence\":\"I reproduced this. It is a real but low-severity documentation error, and it is narrower than the finding says.\\n\\n1. I ran settleLayout from dist with the props in variants/a/extra/ten.props.json and long.props.json, and counted the distinct badge y values:\\n   - ten at 1920x1080: 2 rows, y=759/861, 5+5.\\n   - ten at 1080x1080: 2 rows, 5+5.\\n   - ten at 1080x1920: 2 rows, 5+5.\\n   - ten at 1280x720: 1 row. All ten badges have y=528 (badgePx 26, captionPx 11).\\n   - long at 1920x1080: 1 row of 6, y=762 (badgePx 76).\\n   - long at 1080x1080 and 1080x1920: 2 rows, 3+3.\\n2. I opened extra/ten-1280x720.png. All ten badges sit in one row (25 50 100 250 500 1000 in green, then 25 50 100 250 in grey). extra/long-1920x1080.png also shows six badges in one row.\\n3. 30-build.md lines 51-52 say \\\"`ten`: 10 clubs at 1920x1080, 1080x1080, 1080x1920 and 1280x720. Two rows of 5\\\". That is false for the 1280x720 render, which is a claim not true in the picture.\\n\\nLimits on the finding:\\n- **Brief rule:** the break from the brief's \\\"At most 5 per row\\\" (brief line 150, table lines 262-263) is disclosed in general terms. 30-build.md lines 118-119 say: \\\"on a wide band the card may use one row of n when that draws the badges larger (it chose two rows at 1920x1080)\\\". The source comment (line 587) and the WHY text (line 728: \\\"two rows, or one long row on a wide card\\\") say the same. So the one-row behaviour is a disclosed departure. What is wrong is the build log's description of the 1280x720 render.\\n- **The `long` half:** line 57 reads \\\"a 40-character name wraps to two lines in portrait, with ... six clubs (3 + 3)\\\". That is anchored to portrait, and portrait really is 3+3. Calling it false is a stretch; at most the sentence is incomplete about the 1920x1080 one-row render.\\n\\nFix: in the `ten` bullet, say that 1280x720 is one row of 10.\"}}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"key\":\"v2:a7730e33bb85990f38e76376d914b680104256658c14762c06a5252e6624fc55\",\"agentId\":\"aadb4847ab36ac6c9\",\"result\":{\"real\":true,\"evidence\":\"I reproduced the finding and the build log does not disclose it.\\n\\n1) I ran a node sweep of settleLayout from dist/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.js with 1 to 10 clubs ('1xR25,...'):\\n   - At 480x270, 1 to 7 clubs work. 8, 9 and 10 clubs throw \\\"milestones cannot be fitted on 480x270 above the 6px readability floor\\\".\\n   - At 640x360, only 10 clubs fail.\\n   - At 1280x720 and every larger contract canvas, all counts work.\\n\\n2) I repeated this with realistic counts on all seven CONTRACT_CANVASES, for example eight = '4xR25,3xR50,1xR100,2xR250,1xR500,1xR1000,2xV25,1xV50':\\n   - Eight and nine clubs are refused only at 480x270.\\n   - Seven clubs fit there with a 6px caption, and six clubs with a 7px caption.\\n\\n3) I ran the CLI: m0saic make @one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1 -w 480 -h 270 with the eight-club props file journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/eight-clubs.props.json. It exits 1 with the same \\\"milestones cannot be fitted on 480x270\\\" error.\\n\\n4) What the template claims:\\n   - The WHY caveat (src line 728, and visible on variants/a/stills/tutorial-3.png) reads: \\\"From six clubs the badges get smaller ...; ten clubs need 1280x720 or larger and are refused on the 640x360 and 480x270 thumbnails.\\\"\\n   - The outputHints note (line 747) says \\\"Ten milestone clubs need 1280x720 or larger.\\\"\\n   - The milestones prop description (line 154) says \\\"Up to 10 entries\\\" and gives no canvas limit.\\n   - The test comment (line 106) says only ten clubs are refused at the thumbnails.\\n   Together these imply that 8 or 9 clubs render on every canvas, and they do not at 480x270.\\n\\n5) journal/2026-10-06/30-build.md discloses only \\\"Ten clubs refuse at 640x360 and 480x270\\\" (in Departures, and in the 'ten' stress render). It says nothing about 8 or 9 clubs being refused at 480x270. The brief (20-brief.md) expects 0 to 10 clubs to work.\\n\\nThis is a low-severity real defect: what the card says on screen is untrue for 8 or 9 clubs at 480x270, and the build log does not disclose it.\"}}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"key\":\"v2:6cb63f45c121dcfbe1c04163b514795d755231017731092dc3ce412ba85b1859\",\"agentId\":\"aa94bcf16362dba09\",\"result\":{\"real\":false,\"evidence\":\"The measurements are correct, but they don't break any claim or brief rule, so this is not a real defect.\\n\\nWhat I ran: `node` with `settleLayout(props, W, H).L` from dist. With default props it gives hero/stat/badge px of:\\n- 1920x1080: 109/68/76\\n- 3840x2160: 221/138/153\\n- 1280x720: 73/45/51\\n- 480x270: 27/16/20\\n- 1080x1080: 140/87/69\\n- 1080x1920: 211/130/68\\n\\nIn variants/a/stills/landscape.png the badge numbers 25/50/100 do look taller than 38/27/19.\\n\\nWhy this is not a defect:\\n1. The header comment (lines 20-22) says the four stat tiles' numbers \\\"are capped at 1/1.6 of the headline numbers, so the hierarchy holds on every canvas\\\". That is true: 68/109 = 1.60, enforced at line 535. The hierarchy it means is the ONE CONCEPT \\\"two numbers carry the week\\\", headline over the four tiles. The comment never puts the badges in a tier below the stats.\\n2. The same scope appears everywhere else. Line 534: \\\"a stat number is never more than 1/1.6 of a headline number\\\". The WHY solution (line 682) and the test at line 111 (\\\"headline numbers are at least 1.5x the stat numbers\\\") say the same. None of them says anything about badge size relative to stat numbers.\\n3. The brief has no such rule either. Rubric 1 asks only that the hero numbers be \\\"clearly the largest text on the card at every canvas (at least 1.5x the stat values)\\\". The badge spec only says \\\"the club number big and a caption below\\\". I checked default, one-club (`1xR1000`), two-club and all-9999 props on 1920x1080, 1280x720, 480x270, 1080x1080, 1080x1920, 3840x2160 and 1440x1080. The hero number is the largest text in every case: hero/badge is at least 1.35, and hero/stat is at least 1.5. So rubric 1 holds.\\n4. 30-build.md says \\\"214 finishers and 31 volunteers ... the largest text on every canvas\\\", which is also true in the picture.\\n\\nCalling the badges a \\\"third tier\\\" that must sit below the stat numbers is the reviewer's own design reading, not a stated rule. At most it is a style point, not wrong output or a false claim.\"}}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"key\":\"v2:403289cb46488299691ab3af7d5b43f17942fb2df9dce1cd5812eeab7cc241cd\",\"agentId\":\"a3b07ed1f1db4a43b\",\"result\":{\"real\":false,\"evidence\":\"The behaviour reproduces, but it follows the brief and the repo's conventions, so it is not a defect of this template.\\n\\nWhat I ran: the reviewer's command with journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/typo.props.json (top-level `count` and `milestone` misspelled), output to scratch/review/typo-verify.png. It exits 0 with no warning. The picture shows RIVERSIDE 5K, #88, SAT 10 OCT 2026, the sample counts 214/31/38/27/19/4, the sample badges and the custom footer. A node call against dist confirms it: normalizeWeeklyRunReport({eventName:'X',count:{finishers:1}}) returns the DEFAULT_COUNTS, the same as normalizeWeeklyRunReport({}).\\n\\nWhy it is not a defect:\\n1) The brief asks for this. 20-brief.md's props table gives `counts` the default {214,38,27,19,31,4} and `milestones` the default \\\"4xR25, 3xR50, 1xR100, 2xV25\\\". It also says \\\"All props are optional and every default renders a full card.\\\" So a card with `counts` left out is meant to show the sample counts. A misspelled top-level key is the same case to the template, because it never receives a `counts` value.\\n2) The refusals the brief asks for are at the count-key level, and they all work. Brief rules and rubric 2 list: unknown counts key, missing key, PBs above finishers, bad club, duplicate club, 11 badges, bad date. In node, counts missing 'firstTimeVolunteers' is refused with \\\"...The card never invents a number.\\\", and counts with 'newPb' is refused as an unknown key. Nowhere does the brief ask for unknown top-level props to be refused.\\n3) The header comment's claim (lines 26-30) is about count keys and it is true. It reads \\\"A count key it does not know, a missing key, more new PBs than finishers or a club that does not exist is refused\\\". \\\"A missing key\\\" refers to a count key, and the \\\"never invents a number\\\" message belongs to the missing-count-key error. \\\"Prints what was typed and nothing else\\\" sits next to \\\"fetches nothing, derives no percentage, no record and no ranking\\\", which is about derived values, not defaults.\\n4) The whole repo does this. AGENTS.md asks for \\\"typed props with deterministic defaults\\\" and says \\\"Every optional prop shows its default\\\". The same `{ ...DEFAULTS, ...props }` merge, with no check for unknown top-level keys, appears in qsl-card, radio-top-30-chart, cubing-average-card, swim-time-drop-card, bird-walk-sightings and homebrew-serving-card. It is a CLI/platform behaviour, not a validation hole this template added or a brief rule it broke.\\n\\nRefusing unknown top-level props could be a useful improvement across the repo, but it does not count as a defect today under the review criteria.\"}}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"key\":\"v2:191729cb51caf5050ca1585e68067052cffde730c525cd020347eb5738278aac\",\"agentId\":\"a6abad53693714aa1\",\"result\":{\"real\":true,\"evidence\":\"I reproduced it. The date half is a real defect. The footer half is weaker, because the tutorial's own fourth tip covers it.\\n\\nWhat I ran:\\n1. I rendered `journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/tutorial-week.props.json` with m0saic make at 1080x1080 to `journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/verify-tutorial-week.png`. That file is the tutorial's example, `{\\\"eventName\\\":\\\"Your Park 5k\\\",\\\"runNumber\\\":313,\\\"counts\\\":{...},\\\"milestones\\\":\\\"2xR25, 1xV50\\\"}`, with counts filled in.\\n2. The PNG header reads \\\"YOUR PARK 5K / #313 | SAT 03 OCT 2026\\\". The footer reads \\\"Sample week: event and numbers are invented\\\".\\n3. A node check gave the same result: `normalizeWeeklyRunReport(props)` returns runText `#313`, date `SAT 03 OCT 2026` and footer `\\\"Sample week: event and numbers are invented\\\"`.\\n\\nCause:\\n- In `src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts`, `normalizeWeeklyRunReport` (line 273) fills every missing prop from `DEFAULTS` (lines 83-91).\\n- So when date is left out, the sample run's date, `\\\"2026-10-03\\\"`, appears next to the user's run #313. That date belongs to run #312, a week before #313.\\n\\nWhat the tutorial says:\\n- The tutorial (`WHY.usage.try[0]`, line 687, visible on `variants/a/stills/tutorial-4.png`) gives that week.json as the way to make your own week's card.\\n- None of the four tips mentions the date prop.\\n- The solution text says \\\"It prints what was typed\\\".\\n- So following the tutorial puts a date the user never typed on the card, and it is the wrong date for that run.\\n\\nMitigations:\\n- Defaulting the date is what the brief asks for: the props table in `20-brief.md` gives date the default `\\\"2026-10-03\\\"` and says \\\"All props are optional\\\". The code follows the brief here.\\n- The footer part is mostly covered: `try[3]` says `footer \\\"\\\"` removes the sample line.\\n- The try line is an abbreviated sketch (`counts:{...}`) with a 110-character budget (`src/_shared/why.ts`, `maxTryChars`).\\n\\nStill a defect:\\n- Nothing in `30-build.md` mentions this. Its departures cover the event name fit ladder, ten clubs and square tiles.\\n- The tutorial gives no hint about the date. A user who copies the example gets a card with the wrong date and no error.\\n\\nI'd call it low-to-medium severity, not medium. The fix is to put date in the example, for instance by dropping eventName to stay under 110 characters, or to mention date in another tip.\"}}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"key\":\"v2:8e42e7d2ab785e7892800a6e217d8399be8c9a81b5dc76fe47006b1411903343\",\"agentId\":\"a79c927819aed729f\",\"result\":{\"real\":true,\"evidence\":\"I reproduced this in code and in a render. It is not disclosed in 30-build.md.\\n\\n1. Code. Running `node -e` against `dist/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.js`, `normalizeWeeklyRunReport({counts:{finishers:40,newPbs:5,firstTimers:3,visitors:2,volunteers:8,firstTimeVolunteers:1}, milestones:'90xR25, 30xV25'})` returns without error. It gives milestones `[{kind:'R',club:25,count:90,caption:'90 runners'},{kind:'V',club:25,count:30,caption:'30 volunteers'}]` and counts finishers 40, volunteers 8. A related input with newPbs 30 and firstTimers 30 on 40 finishers is also accepted.\\n\\n2. Picture. `m0saic make ... -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/msum.props.json -o journal/2026-10-06/scratch/review/msum.png` exits 0. The still shows hero numbers `40 finishers` and `8 volunteers`, with a green badge `25 / 90 runners` and a grey badge `25 / 30 volunteers` under MILESTONE CLUBS. That week is impossible, and it is drawn as fact.\\n\\n3. Why it counts as a defect:\\n   - The template's own `milestones` description (schema, ~line 150) says these are \\\"The milestone clubs reached this week\\\". The scout describes runstats as \\\"the stats of the latest run\\\". So every R-club runner finished this run and every V-club volunteer volunteered at it, which means sum(R counts) <= finishers and sum(V counts) <= volunteers.\\n   - `parseCounts` (lines 250-254) does refuse the same kind of cross-field impossibility for newPbs, firstTimers and visitors against finishers, and firstTimeVolunteers against volunteers. The header comment (lines 27-30) gives the reason: \\\"a silently ignored typo puts a wrong number on a public page\\\".\\n   - `parseMilestones` (lines 213-234) and `normalizeWeeklyRunReport` (~line 290) never compare milestone counts with `counts`. They only check that each count is 1-999.\\n   - Rubric 2 in the brief says \\\"Every bad input is refused with a message that names the field and the value\\\".\\n\\n4. Mitigation, which makes it lower severity than \\\"medium\\\". The brief's explicit milestone rules (club set, counts 1-999, at most 10 entries, no duplicates) are all implemented. The cross-check is not one of the brief's listed refusals, so no listed rule is broken. It is an unrefused-impossible-input hole, not a departure from the brief. 30-build.md has no disclosure of it: I checked \\\"Departures from the brief\\\" and the caveats.\\n\\n5. The newPbs + firstTimers > finishers point is weaker. Those two flags do look mutually exclusive on results pages, but the build's own `maxed` stress props (all counts 9999) would break that rule, so I base the verdict on the milestone-sum hole.\"}}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"key\":\"v2:258c8d1ff81fcf696c07c5c18a0521cd4b49a43a79c6f5b1978f9c4ff4ea9abc\",\"agentId\":\"a0e88aa623c3be9de\",\"result\":{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Six milestone clubs render as one row of 6 on every wide canvas: breaks the brief's '6 entries -> 3 + 3' vector and 'at most 5 per row'; 30-build.md discloses this only for ten clubs and says the long set shows 3 + 3\",\"file\":\"src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts\",\"repro\":\"node: settleLayout({milestones:'6xR25, 4xR50, 3xR100, 2xR250, 1xR500, 5xV25'}, W, H).L.badges, rows grouped by rect.y. 1920x1080 gives [6], and so do 1280x720, 3840x2160, 640x360 and 480x270; only 1080x1080 and 1080x1920 give [3,3]. 1920x1080 draws six 216x180 badges in one row. The build's own still journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/extra/long-1920x1080.png shows the six clubs in ONE row, but 30-build.md says '`long`: ... six clubs (3 + 3)'. Expected (brief, Milestone badges and Test vectors): 'At most 5 per row: 6-10 badges make two rows of ceil(n/2) and floor(n/2)' and '6 entries | two rows, 3 + 3'. The only disclosed departure is headed 'Ten clubs: on a wide band the card may use one row of n'. The cause is line 588: the `arrange([n], n)` option is offered on wide for any n >= 6, and it wins whenever its captions come out larger. The test checks rows(SIX) only at 1080x1080.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"suggestedFix\":\"Either cap the wide one-row option at 5 (offer arrange([n], n) only when n <= 5, i.e. never for 6-10), or keep the behaviour and fix 30-build.md: make the departure cover 6-10 clubs, not just ten, and correct the 'long ... six clubs (3 + 3)' line to say 3 + 3 on square/portrait and one row of 6 on wide. Add a test row for SIX at 1920x1080 that pins whichever rule is chosen.\"},{\"title\":\"30-build.md says ten clubs at 1280x720 make 'two rows of 5'; the render and the code put all ten in one row with 11px captions\",\"file\":\"journal/2026-10-06/30-build.md\",\"repro\":\"30-build.md stress section: '`ten`: 10 clubs at 1920x1080, 1080x1080, 1080x1920 and 1280x720. Two rows of 5'. journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/extra/ten-1280x720.png shows ONE row of 10 badges. dist agrees: settleLayout({milestones: TEN}, 1280, 720) gives 1 row of 80x80 badges, club 26px, caption 11px (page floor 16). 3840x2160 is also one row of 10. Expected: the claim should match the picture. The brief's test vector is '10 entries | two rows, 5 + 5'.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"suggestedFix\":\"Correct the stress line in 30-build.md: two rows of 5 at 1920x1080, 1080x1080 and 1080x1920; one row of 10 at 1280x720 and 3840x2160, with captions at 11px on 1280x720. Or drop the one-row option so the 5 + 5 claim and the brief's vector both hold.\"},{\"title\":\"The WHY 'Use it' example renders a real week with the sample date and the 'event and numbers are invented' footer\",\"file\":\"src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts\",\"repro\":\"WHY.usage.try[0] is week.json {\\\"eventName\\\":\\\"Your Park 5k\\\",\\\"runNumber\\\":313,\\\"counts\\\":{...},\\\"milestones\\\":\\\"2xR25, \n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:1c9670f14bbeca40316696494bfb5bb9de8c2c95013fbdd3dc08240850b9e157\",\"agentId\":\"a125328f125b1b1a5\",\"label\":\"verify:brief:Six milestone clubs render as one row of\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:bae3518f4cf61e6221d695a9dc610aabc79ae62e51db41e07340bc17eef1ad51\",\"agentId\":\"a72391f03157af0ff\",\"label\":\"verify:brief:30-build.md says ten clubs at 1280x720 m\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:eb74d79de9c462eca0e976ead2038064dfa422edbf88205b23219b5d2bc3a95e\",\"agentId\":\"afcedc80cf94753bf\",\"label\":\"verify:brief:The WHY 'Use it' example renders a real\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:7cbf8ca7d13e094f15cbc56dbc5d4fc6b7465bb18e217c0febc1d7ba2a9f6e1c\",\"agentId\":\"a09b9d87c28f02828\",\"label\":\"verify:brief:Milestone counts are not checked against\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:4620c4a30e8b226e85ded7d86990687d51e2285d2f442db5a78fe6226efc4980\",\"agentId\":\"a634c3b46eb6faf77\",\"label\":\"verify:brief:footer has a 70-character cap the brief\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:4bc5a9db64db3fae4beb717ddd9d1518bb0f070771ec05409da120ce5cdf3e22\",\"agentId\":\"a561ad376170edfba\",\"label\":\"verify:brief:'first-time volunteers' is one line on w\",\"phase\":\"Verify\"}\n=====\n{\"type\":\"started\",\"key\":\"v2:bd237f4b71f9ddcef9b1aab9328589361f33ac3ac2dac260df8fa44cfacf1463\",\"agentId\":\"a9b2bbdd10c7195a5\",\"label\":\"verify:brief:With footer \\\"\\\" the freed height goes int\",\"phase\":\"V